SUMMARY:Mosses of Duke Gardens
DESCRIPTION:Walk the Gardens with Blanka Aguero\, bryophyte data manager at the Duke University Herbarium\, to look for mosses and liverworts\, discussing what they tell you about the site. Visit and learn about recent expansions to the moss garden that have increased the variety of mosses you’ll encounter here. You will learn identifying characteristics of these small plants by observing similarities and differences with a magnifying lens. \nFee: $24; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Fees apply. \nLocation: Onsite at Duke Gardens. Meeting location will be included in a program reminder email sent the week before the program. \nAccessibility: This will be a small group program that takes place seated indoors and outdoors and traveling on a combination of paved and unpaved paths with some uneven surfaces and moderate inclines.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/botany-spotlight-mosses-of-duke-gardens/
LOCATION:Onsite at Duke Gardens – directions to follow
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Bodine_Asiatic_Moss-Garden-0757.jpg
