SUMMARY:Botanical Linocut Printmaking
DESCRIPTION:Gather inspiration from the gardens in this introduction to linocut printmaking\, a relief printing technique where an image is carved into a linoleum block\, with Bella Insignares\, education staff at Duke Gardens. Participants will have the opportunity to make prints from nature\, practice relief printmaking and carve their own linocut stamp. \nFee: $36; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Fees apply. \nLocation: Onsite at Duke Gardens. Meeting location will be included in a program reminder email sent the week before the program. \nAccessibility: This program will take place seated indoors\, in a location accessible by fully paved paths.
