SUMMARY:Water Features from Bird Baths to Ponds
DESCRIPTION:Landscape water features are a feast for the eyes\, and the sound of water cascading from a fountain or waterfall can be quite relaxing. The class presented by Sheldon Galloway\, Owner and Head of Operations at Garden Environments\, will talk about types of water features and the benefits of adding one to your garden. \nFee: Free\, registration recommended. \nLocation: Stanford L. Warren Library \nRegister at https://go.ncsu.edu/hattiemeadows \nThis program is part of the Hattie Meadows Gardening School\, a free community learning project to spread knowledge and love of gardening. Classes will take place at the Stanford L. Warren Library from January through June 2026. This program is presented in partnership with Stanford L. Warren Library\, Sarah P. Duke Gardens and Durham County Cooperative Extension and made possible by the Durham Library Foundation.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/water-features-from-bird-baths-to-ponds/
LOCATION:Durham County Library\, Stanford L. Warren Branch\, 1201 Fayetteville St.\, Durham\, NC\, 27707\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Hattie.png
END:VEVENT
