SUMMARY:Tabletop Topiary Therapy: the Gibson Method to Creative Pruning
DESCRIPTION:Join renowned topiary artist Michael P. Gibson\, former artist-in-residence of the legendary Pearl Fryar and founder of Gibson Works Property Art\, for an immersive\, hands-on workshop that blends artistry with therapeutic horticulture. Learn the eight principles of the Gibson Method to Contemporary Topiary as you design\, shape\, refine and bring your own unique tabletop topiary vision to life. With personalized\, one‑on‑one guidance from Gibson\, experience how creative pruning can nurture both artistic expression and emotional well‑being. Each participant will receive a two-foot-tall evergreen shrub. \nFee: $88; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nLocation: SEEDS\, 706 Gilbert St.\, Durham\n \nAccessibility: This will be a small group program that takes place seated indoors or outdoors (weather dependent)\, in a location that requires traveling on an uneven mowed grass surface. \nPhoto courtesy of Gibson Works LLC
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/tabletop-topiary-therapy-the-gibson-method-to-creative-pruning/
LOCATION:SEEDS\, 706 Gilbert Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Gibson-Works-LLC.jpg
END:VEVENT
